[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver_multi/lib/semver_range_impl.py: In _compile_clause (lines 145-154) the hyphen-range branch calls _parse_version_text directly on both operands, bypassing the bare-partial-version validation that _expand_term applies to every other comparator form. Per the POSTCONDITIONS of low/semver_range.pyi, a hyphen expression supplying bare partial versions lacking wildcard characters (such as '1.2 - 2.3') MUST raise semver_range.InvalidRangeError; instead the operand '1.2' is forwarded as-is to the version engine parser, which raises an undeclared IndexError, so callers receive an unexpected exception instead of the contracted InvalidRangeError postcondition. Hyphen operands must be routed through the same complete-version-or-wildcard validation and wildcard expansion path as ordinary comparator terms so the contracted InvalidRangeError is produced for bare partial operands.
