[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver_multi/tests/dependency_solver_impl_test.py: Coverage of the contracted search behavior in dependency_solver.resolve is incomplete: the dependency_solver_impl.pyi grounding and the backtracking_solver_ext Assignment & Forward Checking mechanics require a scenario where a candidate release declares a dependency on an already assigned package whose version violates that dependency's range, causing the conflict to be recorded against the involved packages in the conflict trail and backtracking to the next lower-precedence candidate, and require a scenario where a package that has viable candidates exhausts every candidate branch so the failure is recorded and the root search raises ResolutionConflictError with a composed explanation. The existing cases only exercise the empty-candidate-list path and an assignment order that always decides the constrained package after all of its requesters, so the conflicting-assigned-package conflict path and the exhausted-candidate-loop failure path are never exercised. Add public resolve scenarios covering a conflict against an already assigned package that backtracks to a compatible lower-precedence release, and a scenario where every candidate branch fails and ResolutionConflictError is raised, per the contracted postconditions.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver_multi/tests/semver_core_impl_test.py: The compare_precedence postconditions in semver_core.pyi are only half exercised: existing cases assert only the v1 < v2 direction and never assert the symmetric v1 > v2 direction, and no case asserts zero for semantically equal pre-release sequences or for equal numeric pre-release identifiers. The specification requires compare_precedence to return a positive integer when v1 > v2 and zero when v1 == v2, to compare pre-release segments numerically when both are numeric and ASCII-lexicographically when both are string, to rank numeric identifiers below string identifiers, and to rank a longer pre-release sequence above its matching common prefix. Add public parse_version/compare_precedence scenarios covering the greater-than direction for numeric and for alphanumeric pre-release identifiers, a string identifier compared against a numeric identifier in the direction where the string outranks the numeric, equal numeric identifiers yielding zero, a longer pre-release sequence supplied as the first argument, and identical pre-release sequences yielding zero for precedence equality under SemVer 2.0.0.
